column2:
-e / --execute belongs to the mysql CLIENT, not docker. Runs the SQL and exits
(no interactive prompt). Multiple statements separated by ;

  docker compose exec mysql mysql -u root -padmin mydb -e "SHOW TABLES;"
                       (service)  (client)             (mysql's flag)

Non-interactive output is TAB-separated. For the ASCII grid add -t/--table;
for vertical rows end the statement with \G instead of ;
